{
  "bookId": "GEN",
  "chapter": 10,
  "bookEnglish": "Genesis",
  "bookChineseSimplified": "创世记",
  "bookChineseTraditional": "創世記",
  "verses": [
    {
      "verse": "1",
      "en": {
        "text": "Now this is the history of the generations of the sons of Noah and of Shem, Ham, and Japheth. Sons were born to them after the flood.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "的儿子、、的后代记在下面。洪水以后，他们都生了儿子。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "的兒子、、的後代記在下面。洪水以後，他們都生了兒子。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "2",
      "en": {
        "text": "The sons of Japheth were: Gomer, Magog, Madai, Javan, Tubal, Meshech, and Tiras.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "的儿子是、、、、、、。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "的兒子是、、、、、、。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "3",
      "en": {
        "text": "The sons of Gomer were: Ashkenaz, Riphath, and Togarmah.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "的儿子是、、。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "的兒子是、、。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "4",
      "en": {
        "text": "The sons of Javan were: Elishah, Tarshish, Kittim, and Dodanim.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "的儿子是、、、。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "的兒子是、、、。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "5",
      "en": {
        "text": "Of these were the islands of the nations divided in their lands, everyone after his language, after their families, in their nations.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "这些人的后裔将各国的地土、海岛分开居住，各随各的方言、宗族立国。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "這些人的後裔將各國的地土、海島分開居住，各隨各的方言、宗族立國。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "6",
      "en": {
        "text": "The sons of Ham were: Cush, Mizraim, Put, and Canaan.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "的儿子是、、、。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "的兒子是、、、。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "7",
      "en": {
        "text": "The sons of Cush were: Seba, Havilah, Sabtah, Raamah, and Sabteca. The sons of Raamah were: Sheba and Dedan.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "的儿子是、、、、。的儿子是、。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "的兒子是、、、、。的兒子是、。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "8",
      "en": {
        "text": "Cush became the father of Nimrod. He began to be a mighty one on the earth.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "又生，他为世上英雄之首。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "又生，他為世上英雄之首。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "9",
      "en": {
        "text": "He was a mighty hunter before the LORD. Therefore it is said, “like Nimrod, a mighty hunter before the LORD”.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "他在耶和华面前是个英勇的猎户，所以俗语说：「像在耶和华面前是个英勇的猎户。」",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "他在耶和華面前是個英勇的獵戶，所以俗語說：「像在耶和華面前是個英勇的獵戶。」",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "10",
      "en": {
        "text": "The beginning of his kingdom was Babel, Erech, Accad, and Calneh, in the land of Shinar.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "他国的起头是、、、，都在地。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "他國的起頭是、、、，都在地。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "11",
      "en": {
        "text": "Out of that land he went into Assyria, and built Nineveh, Rehoboth Ir, Calah,",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "他从那地出来往去，建造、、，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "他從那地出來往去，建造、、，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "12",
      "en": {
        "text": "and Resen between Nineveh and the great city Calah.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "和、中间的，这就是那大城。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "和、中間的，這就是那大城。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "13",
      "en": {
        "text": "Mizraim became the father of Ludim, Anamim, Lehabim, Naphtuhim,",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "生人、人、人、人、",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "生人、人、人、人、",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "14",
      "en": {
        "text": "Pathrusim, Casluhim (which the Philistines descended from), and Caphtorim.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "人、人、人；从出来的有人。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "人、人、人；從出來的有人。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "15",
      "en": {
        "text": "Canaan became the father of Sidon (his firstborn), Heth,",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "生长子，又生",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "生長子，又生",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "16",
      "en": {
        "text": "the Jebusites, the Amorites, the Girgashites,",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "和人、人、人、",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "和人、人、人、",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "17",
      "en": {
        "text": "the Hivites, the Arkites, the Sinites,",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "人、人、人、",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "人、人、人、",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "18",
      "en": {
        "text": "the Arvadites, the Zemarites, and the Hamathites. Afterward the families of the Canaanites were spread abroad.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "人、人、人，后来的诸族分散了。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "人、人、人，後來的諸族分散了。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "19",
      "en": {
        "text": "The border of the Canaanites was from Sidon—as you go toward Gerar—to Gaza—as you go toward Sodom, Gomorrah, Admah, and Zeboiim—to Lasha.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "的境界是从向的路上，直到，又向、、、的路上，直到。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "的境界是從向的路上，直到，又向、、、的路上，直到。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "20",
      "en": {
        "text": "These are the sons of Ham, after their families, according to their languages, in their lands and their nations.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "这就是的后裔，各随他们的宗族、方言，所住的地土、邦国。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "這就是的後裔，各隨他們的宗族、方言，所住的地土、邦國。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "21",
      "en": {
        "text": "Children were also born to Shem (the elder brother of Japheth), the father of all the children of Eber.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "的哥哥，是子孙之祖，他也生了儿子。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "的哥哥，是子孫之祖，他也生了兒子。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "22",
      "en": {
        "text": "The sons of Shem were: Elam, Asshur, Arpachshad, Lud, and Aram.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "的儿子是、、、、。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "的兒子是、、、、。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "23",
      "en": {
        "text": "The sons of Aram were: Uz, Hul, Gether, and Mash.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "的儿子是、、、。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "的兒子是、、、。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "24",
      "en": {
        "text": "Arpachshad became the father of Shelah. Shelah became the father of Eber.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "生；生。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "生；生。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "25",
      "en": {
        "text": "To Eber were born two sons. The name of the one was Peleg, for in his days the earth was divided. His brother’s name was Joktan.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "生了两个儿子，一个名叫，因为那时人就分地居住；的兄弟名叫。",
        "footnotes": [
          {
            "id": "f1",
            "text": "- 10:25 就是分的意思"
          }
        ],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "生了兩個兒子，一個名叫，因為那時人就分地居住；的兄弟名叫。",
        "footnotes": [
          {
            "id": "f1",
            "text": "- 10:25 就是分的意思"
          }
        ],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "26",
      "en": {
        "text": "Joktan became the father of Almodad, Sheleph, Hazarmaveth, Jerah,",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "生、、、、",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "生、、、、",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "27",
      "en": {
        "text": "Hadoram, Uzal, Diklah,",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "、、、",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "、、、",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "28",
      "en": {
        "text": "Obal, Abimael, Sheba,",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "、、、",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "、、、",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "29",
      "en": {
        "text": "Ophir, Havilah, and Jobab. All these were the sons of Joktan.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "、、，这都是的儿子。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "、、，這都是的兒子。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "30",
      "en": {
        "text": "Their dwelling extended from Mesha, as you go toward Sephar, the mountain of the east.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "他们所住的地方是从直到东边的山。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "他們所住的地方是從直到東邊的山。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "31",
      "en": {
        "text": "These are the sons of Shem, by their families, according to their languages, lands, and nations.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "这就是的子孙，各随他们的宗族、方言，所住的地土、邦国。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "這就是的子孫，各隨他們的宗族、方言，所住的地土、邦國。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "32",
      "en": {
        "text": "These are the families of the sons of Noah, by their generations, according to their nations. The nations divided from these on the earth after the flood.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "这些都是三个儿子的宗族，各随他们的支派立国。洪水以后，他们在地上分为邦国。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "這些都是三個兒子的宗族，各隨他們的支派立國。洪水以後，他們在地上分為邦國。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    }
  ]
}